    "notes": "MODEL: bank -> FCFE at cost of equity through the component engine, the same route as BMO, RY, TD and BNS.TO, so the Canadian banks stay comparable. Deposits are operating funding: net_debt = total_debt = cash = 0. Engine mapping: 'ebitda_margin' = ADJUSTED pre-tax income after provisions for credit losses, less the pre-tax equivalent of preferred/LRCN distributions; SBC and D&A = 0 (already in non-interest expenses); 'capex' = equity retained to keep CET1 at a 13.25% run-rate as the balance sheet grows = (TCE/revenue 1.68) x g/(1+g). TCE/revenue: common equity 31,460 less goodwill 3,101 and intangibles 1,748 (FY2025) = 26.6bn on TTM revenue 15,551 = 1.71 at the 13.5% CET1 reported at Q3 FY2026, scaled to 13.25% = 1.68. FY0 anchors: TTM revenue 15,551 (Q4 FY25 3,698 + 9M FY26 11,853); TTM ADJUSTED pre-tax 6,733 (FY25 5,836 - 9M FY25 4,331 + 9M FY26 5,228) = 43.3% margin, less 1.4pp preferred = 41.9%. Adjusted (not reported) because the excluded items are CWB/LBC integration charges (finite, ~C$250m pre-tax/yr, ending FY2027) and non-cash CWB intangible amortisation. TTM adjusted diluted EPS 12.70 (11.28 - 8.46 + 9.88); reported TTM NI 4,854. last_fcf = TTM adjusted NI to common ~4,971 less retention at 6% growth (1,479) = 3,492 FCFE; reported_fcf holds reported TTM NI to common (4,854 - 165) for audit, there is no bank 'FCF' line. Laurentian retail/SME portfolio purchase (~C$4.1bn loans, close ~Nov 2026) is included in year-1 growth; its capital cost is assumed met from the ~25bp CET1 headroom above 13.25%, so that headroom is NOT credited in an equity bridge.",
